Every offer has a **primary**. Sometimes it also rolls a **side**. You can ignore the side. The pay is worse if you do, but the site still completes.

Things the jar already knows how to ask for:

- Kill a leader
- Clear a pack of mobs
- Hold the site (waves optional)
- Find a marked item
- Take an item off a mob
- Reach a mark
- Break a marked block
- Rescue someone
- Keep a ward alive until the primary is done
- Toss an item into lava, a cauldron, or soul fire
- Open the containers on the site

Finish the primary and the same place might come back as **revenge** after it cools down. That is the “we remember you” pass.

Sites in the jar: outpost, desert pyramid, ruined portal, jungle temple, swamp hut, igloo, monument, mansion, ancient city, mineshaft, shipwreck, trail ruins, trial chambers, stronghold, fortress, bastion.

A ruined portal on Scout is a short hold. The same portal on Legend is a longer fight with worse guests. Same building, different night.
